# Project-local scratch directory, committed through a .gitkeep marker with its
# contents ignored. Use `tmp/` for transient files such as commit messages, draft
# text, scratch scripts and probe outputs. scripts/check.sh fails if anything else
# under tmp/ is tracked.
/tmp/*
!/tmp/.gitkeep

# Local, never-committed material such as credentials, API keys and
# environment-specific notes. Ignored whole, so the directory does not exist in a
# fresh clone. scripts/check.sh fails if anything
# under it is tracked.
/secret/

# Environment files, which usually hold credentials. Commit an example with
# placeholder values instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Agent runtime state and personal settings, local to each contributor and not project
# content. Shared Claude Code configuration, such as .claude/settings.json, skills,
# agents and commands, is not ignored, so a project can commit it deliberately. Codex's
# directory holds host-specific settings, such as a context window, and is ignored
# whole. A project that shares a Codex configuration replaces `.codex/` with
# `.codex/*` and adds `!.codex/config.toml`, since git cannot re-include a file inside
# a directory that is ignored as a whole. Codex 0.164.0 applies that file only when
# the project is marked trusted in the user's own ~/.codex/config.toml.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.cc-writes/
# Claude Code's built-in worktree feature places its worktrees in .claude/worktrees/.
# Without this rule each one shows as untracked content.
.claude/worktrees/
.codex/

# Operating system and editor droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
nvim.log

# Add language and tool entries below, such as build output, dependency
# directories and virtual environments. Write each without a trailing slash, as
# `/target` rather than `/target/`, because scripts/scratch.sh may replace the
# directory with a symbolic link to a scratch volume, and a pattern ending in a slash
# matches only a directory.
